<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14311" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14311</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib35" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[35]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
G. Zhou, H. Pan, Y. LeCun, and L. Pinto.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Dino-wm: World models on pre-trained visual features enable zero-shot planning, 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.04983" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.04983</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib36" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[36]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
V. Micheli, E. Alonso, and F. Fleuret.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Transformers are sample-efficient world models.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <em id="bib.bib36.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">The Eleventh International Conference on Learning Representations</em>, 2023.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=vhFu1Acb0xb" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://openreview.net/forum?id=vhFu1Acb0xb</a>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Quantiative Semantics of STL</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a signal <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> representing a signal starting at time t, the quantitative semantics of satisfaction of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\models\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\models\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are defined inductively as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\mu_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\mu_{c})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu(x_{t})-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu(x_{t})-c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\lnot\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\lnot\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\rho(s_{t},\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\rho(s_{t},\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min(\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{1}),\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min(\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{1}),\rho(s_{t},\varphi_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\text{F}_{[a,b]}(\varphi))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>F</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\text{F}_{[a,b]}(\varphi))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t^{\prime}\in[t+a,t+b]}{\max}\rho(s_{t}^{\prime},\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t^{\prime}\in[t+a,t+b]}{\max}\rho(s_{t}^{\prime},\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\text{G}_{[a,b]}(\varphi))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>G</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(s_{t},\text{G}_{[a,b]}(\varphi))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{t^{\prime}\in[t+a,t+b]}{\min}\rho(s_{t}^{\prime},\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{t^{\prime}\in[t+a,t+b]}{\min}\rho(s_{t}^{\prime},\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>HCD proof</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We rewrite the theorem here for easier comprehension.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{HCD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>HCD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{HCD}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the policy induced by hard-constrained decoding with respect to an STL specification <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a deterministic dynamics model used during decoding. Then the generated trajectory satisfies the specification:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{t+1},\hat{a}_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{T},\hat{a}_{T})\}\models\varphi" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{t+1},\hat{a}_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{T},\hat{a}_{T})\}\models\varphi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where each action <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{a}_{t+k}\sim\pi_{\text{HCD}}(\cdot\mid x_{t+k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>HCD</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{t+k}\sim\pi_{\text{HCD}}(\cdot\mid x_{t+k-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+k}=f(x_{t+k-1},\hat{a}_{t+k})\quad\text{for all }k." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+k}=f(x_{t+k-1},\hat{a}_{t+k})\quad\text{for all }k.</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\raise 2.5pt\vtop{\hbox{\vbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\hbox{$\penalty\vbox{\halign{\hfil{\m@th$#\null$}&{\m@th$\null#$}\hfil\cr\pi_{\text{HCD}}(\hat{a}_{t+k}\mid x_{t+k-1})\hbox{}&amp;\hbox{}=\{0\ |\forall\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\in\mathbb{A},\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}\not\models\varphi\land\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}=f(\hat{x}_{t+k-1},\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\}\crcr}}$}}\kern 20.31006pt\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\vrule width=303.7043pt,height=3.38501pt,depth=3.38501pt\vbox{\kern-3.47221pt\hbox{\kern 1.0pt\hbox{{HCD-Safe}}}\kern-3.47221pt}}}}\kern 20.31006pt\hbox{\kern 87.07912pt\hbox{$\{(x_{t+1},a_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{T},a_{T})\}\models\varphi$}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mpadded voffset="2.5pt"><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top"> 
<span class="ltx_p">
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_bottom"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text">
<span class="ltx_tabular ltx_markedasmath ltx_align_bottom"> 
<span class="ltx_tr"> 
<span class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math alttext="\pi_{\text{HCD}}(\hat{a}_{t+k}\mid x_{t+k-1})\hbox{}" display="inline"><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>HCD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow></mrow></mrow></math></span> 
<span class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math alttext="\hbox{}=\{0\ |\forall\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\in\mathbb{A},\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}\not\models\varphi\land\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}=f(\hat{x}_{t+k-1},\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\}" display="inline"><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false" lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊧̸</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>∧</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></math></span> </span> 
</span></span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:303.7pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-3.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_bottom"> 
<span class="ltx_p"> <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">HCD-Safe</span></span> 
</span></span> 
</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"> <span class="ltx_text"><math alttext="\{(x_{t+1},a_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{T},a_{T})\}\models\varphi" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></math></span></span> 
</span></mtext></mpadded><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\raise 2.5pt\vtop{\hbox{\vbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\hbox{$\penalty\vbox{\halign{\hfil{\m@th$#\null$}&amp;{\m@th$\null#$}\hfil\cr\pi_{\text{HCD}}(\hat{a}_{t+k}\mid x_{t+k-1})\hbox{}&amp;\hbox{}=\{0\ |\forall\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\in\mathbb{A},\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}\not\models\varphi\land\hat{x}_{t+k}^{(i)}=f(\hat{x}_{t+k-1},\hat{a}_{t+k}^{(i)}\}\crcr}}$}}\kern 20.31006pt\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\vrule width=303.7043pt,height=3.38501pt,depth=3.38501pt\vbox{\kern-3.47221pt\hbox{\kern 1.0pt\hbox{{HCD-Safe}}}\kern-3.47221pt}}}}\kern 20.31006pt\hbox{\kern 87.07912pt\hbox{$\{(x_{t+1},a_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{T},a_{T})\}\models\varphi$}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by induction over time. At step <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>, the masking ensures that the selected action <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t+1},a_{t+1})\models\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t+1},a_{t+1})\models\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=f(x_{t},a_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=f(x_{t},a_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that the sequence <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{t+1},a_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{t+k-1},a_{t+k-1})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{t+1},a_{t+1}),\dots,(x_{t+k-1},a_{t+k-1})\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t+k},a_{t+k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t+k},a_{t+k})</annotation></semantics></math> will also satisfy <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>. Since actions are masked based on predicted rollouts using <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is exact, the only permitted actions at step <math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+k</annotation></semantics></math> are those that extend the sequence without violating <math id="A2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>. By induction, the entire sequence satisfies <math id="A2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Robustness weighting ablation</h2>

<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.01728v1/figures/output.png" id="A3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/190;" width="238" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Success rate and STL satisfaction rate across different values of <math id="A3.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for RCD, which controls the importance of STL spcification during decoding. As <math id="A3.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> increases, STL satisfaction improves while task success shows a slight tradeoff beyond moderate values.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the impact of relative weighting between robustness and base logits, we plotted the success rate and STL satisfaction rate across varying values for <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix C Robustness weighting ablation ‣ Constrained Decoding for Robotics Foundation Models constrained-robot-fms.github.io" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, increasing the robustness threshold initially improves both task success and specification satisfaction, with success rates peaking around a moderate threshold (5–10). However, at higher thresholds (20 and 25), success rates begin to decline slightly, while STL satisfaction remains high.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This trend highlights a trade-off introduced by weighting robustness. Higher robustness weighting leads to better STL satisfaction at the cost of hindering overall task completion as logits for feasible actions are shifted heavily by the robustness values. These results demonstrate the importance of carefully balancing robustness weighting to maintain both task success and STL satisfaction.</p>
</div>
</section><div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:creator" content="Anonymous Submission"></div>
